## Summary
The United States has added four Indian companies to its sanctions list targeting entities connected to Iran. The action comes amid the ongoing Middle East conflict and represents a further expansion of US economic restrictions related to Iran.

## Key Points
- The US has sanctioned four additional Indian companies over their connections to Iran
- The sanctions were imposed in the context of the broader Middle East conflict
- This represents a continued expansion of US sanctions targeting entities linked to Iran
- The affected companies are based in India, indicating US scrutiny extends to third-country firms


